1
00:01:30,566 --> 00:01:31,551
=Tigers Sniff the Rose=

2
00:01:31,551 --> 00:01:33,560
(Based on the novel of the same name by Yiren Kuikui)

3
00:01:35,660 --> 00:01:38,260
=Episode 34=

4
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:46,770
We don't have any fine tea to offer.

5
00:01:47,240 --> 00:01:47,850
Just something

6
00:01:48,490 --> 00:01:49,080
to quench your thirst.

7
00:01:50,930 --> 00:01:51,600
You handle that well.

8
00:01:54,240 --> 00:01:55,010
I've done this every day.

9
00:01:55,570 --> 00:01:56,320
I get used to it.

10
00:02:30,530 --> 00:02:32,690
(So you knew
what the poison would do to you.)

11
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:35,880
(That's why you wouldn't listen to me)

12
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:39,160
(and handed over the ledgers.)

13
00:03:00,970 --> 00:03:02,600
Miss, why are you crying?

14
00:03:11,090 --> 00:03:12,850
It's been dry for so long.
The wind carries dust.

15
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:14,370
It keeps blowing right into the eyes.

16
00:03:15,160 --> 00:03:16,320
My eyes have been itching too.

17
00:03:17,410 --> 00:03:19,760
Then why doesn't she ever speak?

18
00:03:24,290 --> 00:03:25,090
My maid

19
00:03:25,810 --> 00:03:26,370
can't speak.

20
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:28,010
You know,

21
00:03:28,530 --> 00:03:29,290
things are different now.

22
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:30,600
In the palace,

23
00:03:31,440 --> 00:03:33,090
we can only trust servants
who can't speak

24
00:03:33,530 --> 00:03:34,160
to attend to us.

25
00:03:35,160 --> 00:03:36,640
Mr. Yan can't see.

26
00:03:37,130 --> 00:03:38,530
This young lady can see,

27
00:03:38,640 --> 00:03:39,970
but she can't speak.

28
00:03:40,290 --> 00:03:41,090
How unfortunate.

29
00:03:41,970 --> 00:03:42,440
Miss,

30
00:03:42,880 --> 00:03:43,880
can you read?

31
00:03:46,880 --> 00:03:48,010
So you can read.

32
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:52,640
Mind your manners.

33
00:03:54,040 --> 00:03:54,530
I'm sorry.

34
00:03:54,760 --> 00:03:55,160
Magistrate.

35
00:03:55,640 --> 00:03:57,480
The well-diggers from east town are here
asking for their pay.

36
00:04:00,290 --> 00:04:00,880
Please wait here.

37
00:04:01,530 --> 00:04:02,370
I'll be right back.

38
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:38,570
I...

39
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:39,250
That's enough.

40
00:04:40,490 --> 00:04:41,050
You don't have to say it.

41
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:42,840
I know what you mean.

42
00:04:43,440 --> 00:04:44,080
What do you know?

43
00:04:44,610 --> 00:04:45,320
You're going to say

44
00:04:46,440 --> 00:04:48,050
your old flame is noble

45
00:04:48,370 --> 00:04:49,010
and honest,

46
00:04:49,760 --> 00:04:50,960
and he'd never embezzle

47
00:04:51,250 --> 00:04:52,050
the relief funds in Lanyang.

48
00:04:52,610 --> 00:04:52,930
So

49
00:04:53,440 --> 00:04:54,320
we have nothing to worry about.

50
00:04:54,610 --> 00:04:55,610
Let's go back to Sheng'an.

51
00:04:56,010 --> 00:04:56,610
Yang Si.

52
00:05:00,730 --> 00:05:01,400
You mean

53
00:05:02,810 --> 00:05:03,570
you want to stay here?

54
00:05:04,370 --> 00:05:05,200
Lanyang is hit hard by drought.

55
00:05:06,880 --> 00:05:07,880
No water for the spring planting.

56
00:05:08,690 --> 00:05:09,960
Shouldn't I stay here

57
00:05:10,610 --> 00:05:11,880
and see how he governs,

58
00:05:12,760 --> 00:05:14,520
and how the people here live?

59
00:05:16,880 --> 00:05:18,320
I'll stay a few more days.

60
00:05:21,280 --> 00:05:21,810
What else

61
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:24,370
would you have me do for you,
Your Highness?

62
00:05:25,050 --> 00:05:25,570
Convince him

63
00:05:26,760 --> 00:05:27,490
to let us stay.

64
00:05:35,170 --> 00:05:35,960
You're staying here?

65
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:39,200
Can't old friends share a room
and talk late into the night?

66
00:05:41,320 --> 00:05:42,570
Yang Si, you're welcome

67
00:05:43,170 --> 00:05:43,880
to stay.

68
00:05:44,490 --> 00:05:45,050
But

69
00:05:45,730 --> 00:05:46,760
my place is rather humble.

70
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:48,050
You might not be comfortable here.

71
00:05:48,490 --> 00:05:49,610
I'm not picky.

72
00:05:50,400 --> 00:05:52,370
Back when I was in the army,
I slept in dirt pits

73
00:05:52,610 --> 00:05:53,520
and huddled in snowdrifts.

74
00:05:54,440 --> 00:05:55,050
To be honest,

75
00:05:55,570 --> 00:05:56,880
I'm worried about the disaster.

76
00:05:57,640 --> 00:05:59,370
I'd like to stay and see
how the people here are doing,

77
00:05:59,840 --> 00:06:02,080
and how you're handling
your post as magistrate.

78
00:06:03,760 --> 00:06:04,570
I see.

79
00:06:06,050 --> 00:06:07,440
You've long been at the heart of power.

80
00:06:07,930 --> 00:06:08,880
It's good you came down

81
00:06:09,370 --> 00:06:09,730
here.

82
00:06:10,930 --> 00:06:11,440
But

83
00:06:12,250 --> 00:06:13,280
the drought has been severe lately.

84
00:06:14,050 --> 00:06:15,280
I'm spread pretty thin right now.

85
00:06:15,930 --> 00:06:16,690
Hope

86
00:06:17,250 --> 00:06:19,170
you don't mind the poor hospitality.

87
00:06:19,610 --> 00:06:20,370
Of course not.

88
00:06:21,080 --> 00:06:22,080
Come on, Shang.

89
00:06:22,520 --> 00:06:23,810
Do you take me for some spoiled brat?

90
00:06:38,840 --> 00:06:39,440
Good morning, Miss.

91
00:06:39,840 --> 00:06:41,280
Mr. Yan has already gone out.

92
00:06:45,810 --> 00:06:46,440
Don't worry.

93
00:06:46,690 --> 00:06:48,059
He went to deliver water to Mr. Sun

94
00:06:48,101 --> 00:06:49,101
in the alley across the street.

95
00:06:49,690 --> 00:06:50,490
He's an old man with no family.

96
00:06:50,640 --> 00:06:51,810
Mr. Yan has been bringing him water
for three years.

97
00:06:51,960 --> 00:06:53,250
He knows the way by heart.

98
00:06:58,170 --> 00:06:59,130
Are you asking me?

99
00:07:00,370 --> 00:07:01,640
There's a charity school next door.

100
00:07:01,840 --> 00:07:03,149
Mr. Yan pays an old scholar
out of his own salary

101
00:07:03,191 --> 00:07:04,421
to teach us to read and write.

102
00:07:04,730 --> 00:07:05,760
He's got quite a few students.

103
00:07:06,370 --> 00:07:07,280
I should go help.

104
00:07:07,840 --> 00:07:08,610
See you later, Miss.

105
00:07:18,840 --> 00:07:19,730
Eat up.

106
00:07:20,010 --> 00:07:20,640
- Come back for more.
- Alright.

107
00:07:20,760 --> 00:07:21,179
Come again next time.

108
00:07:21,221 --> 00:07:21,861
Come on, man.

109
00:07:22,340 --> 00:07:24,110
(County Office)

110
00:07:24,170 --> 00:07:25,170
Come back for more if you need it.

111
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:27,250
Did you bring all the tools?

112
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:28,059
Yes.

113
00:07:28,101 --> 00:07:28,951
We can eat our fill.

114
00:07:29,250 --> 00:07:29,789
We can finally eat our fill.

115
00:07:29,831 --> 00:07:31,239
Don't rush, everyone.
There's enough for all.

116
00:07:31,280 --> 00:07:32,119
No rush. Everyone will get some.

117
00:07:32,161 --> 00:07:33,471
There's enough for everyone.
Here you go.

118
00:07:33,570 --> 00:07:35,400
Good thing
the imperial grain shipment arrived.

119
00:07:35,490 --> 00:07:36,130
Easy there, ma'am.

120
00:07:36,840 --> 00:07:37,690
Come back for more, ma'am.

121
00:07:39,010 --> 00:07:39,880
Thank heaven!

122
00:07:40,010 --> 00:07:41,490
It's rice. It's really rice!

123
00:07:42,370 --> 00:07:42,939
There's enough for all.

124
00:07:42,981 --> 00:07:43,901
There's enough for everyone.

125
00:07:49,690 --> 00:07:50,440
Easy, man.

126
00:07:50,730 --> 00:07:51,840
Easy there. There's plenty.

127
00:07:52,320 --> 00:07:53,059
There's plenty.

128
00:07:53,101 --> 00:07:55,101
If we'd had a drought like this
a few years ago,

129
00:07:55,610 --> 00:07:57,810
this city would've been overrun
with bandits by now.

130
00:07:58,370 --> 00:08:00,440
With Magistrate Yan here,
no one has to go hungry.

131
00:08:00,840 --> 00:08:03,280
The County Office has also given
every household grain and seeds.

132
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:04,880
Lanyang won't fall into chaos.

133
00:08:05,050 --> 00:08:05,370
Right.

134
00:08:05,610 --> 00:08:06,760
Times are tough,

135
00:08:06,930 --> 00:08:08,050
but we'll get through them.

136
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:09,130
That's for sure.

137
00:08:11,280 --> 00:08:12,610
What's the point of fixing all this?

138
00:08:13,520 --> 00:08:14,280
You sure talk too much.

139
00:08:14,760 --> 00:08:16,250
Just listen to Magistrate Yan.

140
00:08:17,050 --> 00:08:18,010
If we don't fix it now,

141
00:08:18,170 --> 00:08:19,370
it'll be too late once the rain comes.

142
00:08:20,050 --> 00:08:20,490
That's right.

143
00:08:20,960 --> 00:08:22,810
If Magistrate Yan hadn't taught us
to store water,

144
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:24,520
we wouldn't have made it

145
00:08:24,810 --> 00:08:25,880
through a drought this bad.

146
00:08:26,250 --> 00:08:26,960
Magistrate!

147
00:08:28,250 --> 00:08:28,930
Magistrate!

148
00:08:31,130 --> 00:08:31,440
Thank you.

149
00:08:31,930 --> 00:08:32,640
Magistrate!

150
00:08:34,520 --> 00:08:35,210
Magistrate!

151
00:08:35,760 --> 00:08:36,330
Magistrate.

152
00:08:36,680 --> 00:08:37,829
My mother and the neighbors

153
00:08:37,871 --> 00:08:38,941
made these shoes for you.

154
00:08:39,490 --> 00:08:41,450
They said Cai returned the wheat seeds.

155
00:08:41,880 --> 00:08:42,730
Thank you so much.

156
00:08:43,160 --> 00:08:44,010
I don't have anything else to offer.

157
00:08:44,160 --> 00:08:45,069
Hope you'll accept them.

158
00:08:45,111 --> 00:08:45,701
You don't have to...

159
00:08:48,520 --> 00:08:49,040
Thank you.

160
00:08:51,730 --> 00:08:52,330
Magistrate!

161
00:08:52,850 --> 00:08:53,450
Magistrate!

162
00:08:53,920 --> 00:08:54,370
Magistrate!

163
00:08:55,090 --> 00:08:55,450
Magistrate.

164
00:08:56,160 --> 00:08:57,250
There's trouble at the water sump
south of town.

165
00:08:57,330 --> 00:08:58,400
They want you to settle the dispute.

166
00:08:58,610 --> 00:08:58,920
Hurry.

167
00:08:59,450 --> 00:08:59,920
Take me there.

168
00:09:00,760 --> 00:09:01,250
Careful, Magistrate.

169
00:10:04,540 --> 00:10:06,380
(Slipshod farming ruins the crops;
careless weeding spoils the harvest.)

170
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:31,280
Yang Si,

171
00:11:32,040 --> 00:11:32,800
why are you still up?

172
00:11:37,040 --> 00:11:37,730
So it's not Yang Si.

173
00:11:38,880 --> 00:11:40,280
You're the young lady?

174
00:11:47,250 --> 00:11:48,040
Thank you, Miss.

175
00:11:49,400 --> 00:11:50,010
It's late.

176
00:11:50,370 --> 00:11:50,850
You should

177
00:11:51,680 --> 00:11:52,640
get some rest.

178
00:12:25,130 --> 00:12:26,250
Sorry to trouble you, Miss.

179
00:12:27,490 --> 00:12:29,040
May I know your name?

180
00:12:35,640 --> 00:12:37,040
(I forgot she couldn't speak.)

181
00:12:55,210 --> 00:12:56,370
Zhaoniang?

182
00:13:14,130 --> 00:13:14,560
Miss,

183
00:13:15,210 --> 00:13:15,920
it's late and the dew is heavy.

184
00:13:16,880 --> 00:13:17,970
You should get some rest.

185
00:13:18,640 --> 00:13:20,010
I can manage the writing myself.

186
00:13:20,880 --> 00:13:21,560
You needn't trouble yourself.

187
00:13:29,330 --> 00:13:29,970
Alright.

188
00:13:30,610 --> 00:13:31,400
Go ahead, Miss.

189
00:13:59,060 --> 00:14:02,520
♪The midsummer breeze blows
soft and sweet♪

190
00:14:03,260 --> 00:14:06,720
♪Fireflies dance freely
through the night♪

191
00:14:07,560 --> 00:14:11,120
♪Chasing the beauty
of this fleeting world♪

192
00:14:11,660 --> 00:14:15,090
♪A thousand lights turn night into day♪

193
00:14:15,920 --> 00:14:19,620
♪Cicada songs mingle with the wine♪

194
00:14:20,260 --> 00:14:24,060
♪Their songs linger
through the passing years♪

195
00:14:24,520 --> 00:14:28,090
♪Life is but a fleeting stay♪

196
00:14:28,520 --> 00:14:31,110
♪How lucky I am
to walk this path with you♪

197
00:14:31,160 --> 00:14:31,560
Thank you.

198
00:14:33,090 --> 00:14:36,690
♪Playing out life's game,
forever by your side♪

199
00:14:37,320 --> 00:14:40,960
♪Innocent years drift gently by♪

200
00:14:41,620 --> 00:14:45,160
♪I thought time might stand still♪

201
00:14:45,320 --> 00:14:48,626
♪Forever at that crossroads♪

202
00:14:48,700 --> 00:14:50,740
(Pray for rain)

203
00:14:50,782 --> 00:14:53,760
♪Watching flowers bloom and fade♪

204
00:14:54,360 --> 00:14:57,920
♪Weathering life's rise and fall♪

205
00:14:58,660 --> 00:15:01,960
♪So wordless tenderness♪

206
00:15:02,660 --> 00:15:06,420
♪Is starlight caught in your eyes♪

207
00:15:07,220 --> 00:15:10,860
♪Watching flowers bloom and fade♪

208
00:15:11,460 --> 00:15:14,860
♪Weathering life's rise and fall♪

209
00:15:15,690 --> 00:15:19,060
♪So wordless tenderness♪

210
00:15:19,720 --> 00:15:23,560
♪Is starlight caught in your eyes♪

211
00:15:48,620 --> 00:15:51,780
(When the sun or moon
is eclipsed, we save it.)

212
00:15:58,360 --> 00:16:02,090
♪When the evening breeze begins to blow♪

213
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:05,820
♪After the letter arrives
and the words are said♪

214
00:16:06,890 --> 00:16:10,440
♪In my dreams,
it's still that same glance♪

215
00:16:10,490 --> 00:16:11,040
Thank you.

216
00:16:11,160 --> 00:16:14,460
♪From the day we first met♪

217
00:16:15,420 --> 00:16:19,020
♪A blush of rouge fills my sleeves♪

218
00:16:19,760 --> 00:16:23,320
♪I climb the tower time and again♪

219
00:16:23,960 --> 00:16:27,490
♪The waters flow;
the moon hangs like a hook♪

220
00:16:28,060 --> 00:16:31,620
♪And so it lasts forever♪

221
00:16:32,690 --> 00:16:36,020
♪Though we're worlds apart,
our hearts stay close♪

222
00:16:36,820 --> 00:16:40,360
♪Innocent years drift gently by♪

223
00:16:41,060 --> 00:16:44,720
♪I wish time could stand still♪

224
00:16:44,820 --> 00:16:48,690
♪Forever at that crossroads♪

225
00:16:49,560 --> 00:16:53,320
♪Watching flowers bloom and fade♪

226
00:16:53,820 --> 00:16:57,220
♪Weathering life's rise and fall♪

227
00:16:58,120 --> 00:17:01,420
♪Where endless time comes to an end♪

228
00:17:02,120 --> 00:17:05,690
♪Moonlight and breeze
fill our boat home♪

229
00:17:06,660 --> 00:17:10,020
♪Golden winds and jade dew return♪

230
00:17:10,920 --> 00:17:14,460
♪The world still blooms as before♪

231
00:17:15,120 --> 00:17:18,660
♪How lucky to roam with you♪

232
00:17:18,710 --> 00:17:22,800
♪Back to the road where it all began♪

233
00:17:23,760 --> 00:17:27,020
♪As if our youthful hearts remain♪

234
00:17:28,060 --> 00:17:31,560
♪As if our love will never fade♪

235
00:17:32,220 --> 00:17:38,020
♪Chasing clouds by boat,
carefree and unbound♪

236
00:18:20,890 --> 00:18:21,360
Father.

237
00:18:22,040 --> 00:18:22,890
You're awake.

238
00:18:32,320 --> 00:18:33,520
What are you doing here?

239
00:18:39,120 --> 00:18:40,989
Father, I missed you.

240
00:18:41,031 --> 00:18:42,301
So... so...

241
00:18:43,170 --> 00:18:44,930
I brought your grandson to see you.

242
00:18:53,250 --> 00:18:55,149
Why did you bring him here?

243
00:18:55,191 --> 00:18:56,671
He might catch an illness.

244
00:18:58,210 --> 00:19:00,250
Your Majesty,
all you have is imperial grace.

245
00:19:00,520 --> 00:19:01,360
There's no illness to catch.

246
00:19:03,450 --> 00:19:03,730
Come on.

247
00:19:04,280 --> 00:19:04,730
Call him Grandfather.

248
00:19:05,120 --> 00:19:05,520
Grandfather.

249
00:19:19,320 --> 00:19:20,210
Good boy.

250
00:19:24,170 --> 00:19:26,930
Your Highness,
what's his childhood name?

251
00:19:27,600 --> 00:19:28,450
Si'er.

252
00:19:28,890 --> 00:19:29,730
Si'er?

253
00:19:30,840 --> 00:19:31,120
Come here.

254
00:19:32,040 --> 00:19:33,120
Let Grandfather have a good look.

255
00:19:34,560 --> 00:19:34,840
Come on.

256
00:19:35,120 --> 00:19:36,210
Sit up here on me.

257
00:19:41,800 --> 00:19:42,739
Let me see.

258
00:19:42,781 --> 00:19:44,671
What's that you're playing with?

259
00:19:45,170 --> 00:19:46,730
It's a conch.

260
00:19:48,320 --> 00:19:49,170
Your Majesty,

261
00:19:49,800 --> 00:19:50,800
you look better

262
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:52,690
than ever today.

263
00:19:53,730 --> 00:19:54,650
Your Highnesses,

264
00:19:55,080 --> 00:19:57,010
you really should bring
the little one more often.

265
00:20:01,360 --> 00:20:01,800
Si'er.

266
00:20:02,520 --> 00:20:03,600
Say Grandfather again.

267
00:20:04,280 --> 00:20:04,690
Grandfather!

268
00:20:07,890 --> 00:20:08,800
Look at those little hands.

269
00:20:10,450 --> 00:20:11,250
So chubby.

270
00:20:33,560 --> 00:20:34,490
What's that sound?

271
00:20:34,840 --> 00:20:37,080
The sea. Do you hear the birds?

272
00:20:40,800 --> 00:20:41,730
I do.

273
00:21:09,210 --> 00:21:10,450
It's been three whole years.

274
00:21:14,120 --> 00:21:15,690
Will you still not forgive me?

275
00:21:19,280 --> 00:21:20,690
The Princess Consort of Jin
didn't deserve to die.

276
00:21:22,410 --> 00:21:23,450
She was a pitiful woman too.

277
00:21:26,800 --> 00:21:29,120
But for three years,
every time I held Si'er,

278
00:21:32,280 --> 00:21:33,040
I'd think...

279
00:21:38,520 --> 00:21:40,080
you did all this for me.

280
00:21:44,490 --> 00:21:45,730
How could I blame you?

281
00:22:12,690 --> 00:22:13,120
It's all right.

282
00:22:15,410 --> 00:22:15,800
Chunhua.

283
00:22:19,450 --> 00:22:20,280
Just seeing you is enough.

284
00:22:23,690 --> 00:22:24,040
Even if we

285
00:22:25,650 --> 00:22:26,170
stand here in silence,

286
00:22:30,730 --> 00:22:31,760
I'm happy.

287
00:22:49,080 --> 00:22:50,170
In the few days I've been here,

288
00:22:51,320 --> 00:22:52,250
I've been watching

289
00:22:52,890 --> 00:22:53,690
and doing the sums.

290
00:22:55,450 --> 00:22:56,890
Even if Yan Shang gives it everything,

291
00:22:58,040 --> 00:22:59,730
the relief grain Lanyang gets

292
00:23:00,040 --> 00:23:00,800
is only so much.

293
00:23:02,080 --> 00:23:03,080
It won't last through the eighth month.

294
00:23:03,410 --> 00:23:05,120
Aren't you already planning to
waive the taxes?

295
00:23:06,690 --> 00:23:07,560
Even so,

296
00:23:08,760 --> 00:23:09,650
if it doesn't rain soon,

297
00:23:10,170 --> 00:23:11,010
there'll be no autumn harvest.

298
00:23:12,450 --> 00:23:13,970
The drought stretches so wide.

299
00:23:14,360 --> 00:23:15,410
Every region is struggling.

300
00:23:16,410 --> 00:23:18,650
Borrowing grain from elsewhere
won't work.

301
00:23:19,890 --> 00:23:20,560
When that time comes,

302
00:23:21,730 --> 00:23:22,890
many people will starve to death.

303
00:23:23,280 --> 00:23:23,890
So

304
00:23:24,890 --> 00:23:26,080
Lanyang still has no way out?

305
00:23:26,760 --> 00:23:27,320
I'm afraid

306
00:23:28,840 --> 00:23:29,690
it's not just Lanyang.

307
00:23:40,080 --> 00:23:41,010
- Easy there.
- Has the physician arrived yet?

308
00:23:41,170 --> 00:23:41,650
I'll go hurry him.

309
00:23:41,890 --> 00:23:42,210
Okay.

310
00:23:43,170 --> 00:23:43,760
What happened?

311
00:23:44,690 --> 00:23:45,840
There's only one well left in Lanyang

312
00:23:46,490 --> 00:23:47,320
that hasn't dried up.

313
00:23:48,170 --> 00:23:50,250
Everyone's been struggling these days.

314
00:23:51,250 --> 00:23:52,690
A fight broke out over the well

315
00:23:53,210 --> 00:23:54,010
just now.

316
00:23:55,040 --> 00:23:55,970
In the past two years,

317
00:23:56,040 --> 00:23:58,010
we've hardly had any fights here.

318
00:23:58,250 --> 00:23:59,970
It's all this cursed drought!

319
00:24:00,120 --> 00:24:01,189
- We can go without water,
- Exactly.

320
00:24:01,231 --> 00:24:02,471
but the fields can't.

321
00:24:02,650 --> 00:24:04,210
Otherwise,
we still won't make it to autumn.

322
00:24:04,360 --> 00:24:05,099
Still a dead end.

323
00:24:05,141 --> 00:24:06,471
That's right.

324
00:24:07,970 --> 00:24:09,490
An elder got hurt
trying to break up the fight.

325
00:24:10,280 --> 00:24:11,490
So we carried him here.

326
00:24:12,040 --> 00:24:12,520
Magistrate,

327
00:24:12,930 --> 00:24:14,320
I heard you came third
in the imperial exams.

328
00:24:14,560 --> 00:24:16,890
You're a scholar blessed by the deities.

329
00:24:17,170 --> 00:24:18,840
Surely even Heaven will hear you.

330
00:24:19,170 --> 00:24:20,490
I'm begging you.

331
00:24:20,760 --> 00:24:23,600
Pray for rain for the people of Lanyang.

332
00:24:24,210 --> 00:24:25,210
Please, Magistrate.

333
00:24:25,520 --> 00:24:26,450
Please.

334
00:24:26,600 --> 00:24:29,299
Pray for rain for Lanyang.

335
00:24:29,341 --> 00:24:30,589
We're begging you.

336
00:24:30,630 --> 00:24:32,239
Pray for rain for Lanyang.

337
00:24:32,281 --> 00:24:32,999
We can't survive.

338
00:24:33,041 --> 00:24:34,721
Please, Magistrate.

339
00:24:34,770 --> 00:24:35,319
Ridiculous!

340
00:24:35,361 --> 00:24:35,869
Please.

341
00:24:35,911 --> 00:24:36,671
What good is praying for rain?

342
00:24:37,120 --> 00:24:39,360
It's all superstition,
meant to fool the common folk!

343
00:25:02,320 --> 00:25:03,250
Everyone, get up.

344
00:25:05,800 --> 00:25:06,650
I promise you

345
00:25:07,970 --> 00:25:09,010
I'll set up offerings and an altar

346
00:25:10,280 --> 00:25:11,120
to pray for rain

347
00:25:13,600 --> 00:25:14,450
in Lanyang.

348
00:25:16,450 --> 00:25:20,779
Thank you, Magistrate!

349
00:25:20,821 --> 00:25:21,789
Lanyang still has hope!

350
00:25:21,831 --> 00:25:26,481
Thank you, Magistrate!

351
00:25:26,600 --> 00:25:27,600
Shang, have you lost your mind?

352
00:25:28,320 --> 00:25:29,229
I don't believe you really think

353
00:25:29,271 --> 00:25:30,269
those hocus-pocus rituals

354
00:25:30,311 --> 00:25:31,071
will make it rain!

355
00:25:45,960 --> 00:25:50,450
(Pray, and it rains. Why? No reason.
We pray for rain during droughts.)

356
00:25:50,560 --> 00:25:51,709
Pray for rain, and it rains.

357
00:25:51,751 --> 00:25:52,381
Why?

358
00:25:53,490 --> 00:25:55,010
There's no reason.

359
00:25:55,450 --> 00:25:57,520
It might rain even if you don't pray.

360
00:26:00,320 --> 00:26:00,930
What does that mean?

361
00:26:03,080 --> 00:26:03,970
Praying for rain

362
00:26:04,600 --> 00:26:05,600
has nothing to do

363
00:26:07,280 --> 00:26:08,320
with whether it rains.

364
00:26:09,280 --> 00:26:10,560
That's what Xunzi said.

365
00:26:11,410 --> 00:26:12,410
Then why did you agree

366
00:26:12,730 --> 00:26:13,560
to fool the common folk?

367
00:26:14,170 --> 00:26:15,410
Because the court has done

368
00:26:16,450 --> 00:26:17,280
all it can.

369
00:26:18,600 --> 00:26:20,360
And so have I.

370
00:26:21,490 --> 00:26:22,520
We've done all we can,

371
00:26:23,210 --> 00:26:24,080
but Heaven hasn't answered.

372
00:26:25,210 --> 00:26:25,970
The people of Lanyang

373
00:26:28,080 --> 00:26:28,760
can't wait any longer.

374
00:26:30,600 --> 00:26:32,930
All they want now is a little hope.

375
00:26:33,840 --> 00:26:35,520
I have to give them that.

376
00:26:39,450 --> 00:26:40,800
If they're willing to pray to Heaven,

377
00:26:41,930 --> 00:26:43,410
I'll kneel at the front.

378
00:26:44,410 --> 00:26:45,450
As magistrate of Lanyang,

379
00:26:46,730 --> 00:26:47,970
it's my duty.

380
00:26:49,280 --> 00:26:50,520
As long as the people don't give up,

381
00:26:52,490 --> 00:26:53,600
there's still hope

382
00:26:54,760 --> 00:26:55,760
they'll find a way

383
00:26:57,930 --> 00:26:58,600
to survive.

384
00:27:08,360 --> 00:27:08,930
That's why

385
00:27:10,800 --> 00:27:12,840
I'll hold this rain-praying ceremony
with all due seriousness.

386
00:27:14,840 --> 00:27:15,450
And then?

387
00:27:16,450 --> 00:27:17,010
Then

388
00:27:18,690 --> 00:27:19,760
we wait for a miracle.

389
00:29:23,170 --> 00:29:24,840
In times of drought or flood,
we turn to Heaven.

390
00:29:26,250 --> 00:29:27,650
A failure of governance brings
shame upon officials.

391
00:29:29,250 --> 00:29:30,560
To pray without ceasing

392
00:29:31,690 --> 00:29:33,080
is a blessing to the deities.

393
00:29:34,520 --> 00:29:35,840
If no rain falls within ten days,

394
00:29:36,360 --> 00:29:37,520
the harvest will fail.

395
00:29:38,250 --> 00:29:39,450
The people will go hungry,

396
00:29:40,450 --> 00:29:41,970
and bandits will rise.

397
00:30:18,930 --> 00:30:20,320
We offer fine food and wine,

398
00:30:21,520 --> 00:30:23,170
both in gratitude and in prayer.

399
00:30:24,600 --> 00:30:26,210
May your blessing come.

400
00:30:27,800 --> 00:30:29,800
We pray for an inch of rain.

401
00:31:14,210 --> 00:31:15,520
Where are the deities?

402
00:31:16,360 --> 00:31:18,010
They just sit back and watch, unmoved?

403
00:31:18,730 --> 00:31:20,280
Where are the deities?

404
00:31:21,490 --> 00:31:23,040
They just sit back and watch, unmoved?

405
00:31:24,360 --> 00:31:26,080
Where are the deities?

406
00:31:27,170 --> 00:31:30,010
They just sit back and watch, unmoved?

407
00:31:51,970 --> 00:31:54,970
Summon the deity!

408
00:32:28,180 --> 00:32:29,820
(Chengfu Gate)

409
00:32:41,540 --> 00:32:42,780
(Chengfu Gate)

410
00:32:50,820 --> 00:32:54,120
♪Through thick fog,
the road stretches on♪

411
00:32:54,720 --> 00:32:59,320
♪I've endured every hardship and pain♪

412
00:33:00,120 --> 00:33:02,890
♪Like burning wood, I offer up my flame♪

413
00:33:04,290 --> 00:33:08,120
♪As rain pours down
over a thousand rivers♪

414
00:33:09,560 --> 00:33:14,220
♪I gaze at high peaks
and sails far away♪

415
00:33:14,520 --> 00:33:17,760
♪With the world in my heart,
I leave the shore♪

416
00:33:20,170 --> 00:33:20,560
Sir!

417
00:33:20,970 --> 00:33:21,410
Sir!

418
00:33:21,930 --> 00:33:22,360
Coming through.

419
00:33:22,560 --> 00:33:23,389
What's wrong with the magistrate?

420
00:33:23,431 --> 00:33:23,959
Is he alright?

421
00:33:24,000 --> 00:33:24,749
Is he alright?

422
00:33:24,791 --> 00:33:25,831
- Excuse me.
- Are you alright, sir?

423
00:33:26,410 --> 00:33:26,800
Coming through.

424
00:33:28,040 --> 00:33:28,490
Let's go.

425
00:33:29,600 --> 00:33:29,930
Go!

426
00:33:29,972 --> 00:33:32,160
♪By noon, the mist will lift;
rivers will bend♪

427
00:33:32,210 --> 00:33:34,490
Heaven, please have mercy on us.

428
00:33:35,360 --> 00:33:35,730
No.

429
00:33:36,560 --> 00:33:37,410
We've been at this for half a day.

430
00:33:37,890 --> 00:33:38,560
Keep this up,

431
00:33:39,210 --> 00:33:40,299
people will only die

432
00:33:40,341 --> 00:33:41,271
of heat and exhaustion.

433
00:33:42,650 --> 00:33:43,650
As they say,

434
00:33:44,560 --> 00:33:45,730
walk south to north,

435
00:33:46,890 --> 00:33:47,760
circle the whole city,

436
00:33:48,840 --> 00:33:50,650
and Heaven will see our sincerity.

437
00:33:52,450 --> 00:33:52,970
Fine.

438
00:33:53,520 --> 00:33:54,490
How big can Lanyang be?

439
00:33:55,120 --> 00:33:55,840
Let's keep going.

440
00:33:57,840 --> 00:33:59,210
If it doesn't rain soon,

441
00:34:01,490 --> 00:34:03,450
we're all doomed.

442
00:34:03,650 --> 00:34:05,600
We're on our knees before you.

443
00:34:19,890 --> 00:34:23,010
Open your eyes
and look at us in Lanyang.

444
00:34:26,680 --> 00:34:27,120
Are you alright?

445
00:34:30,370 --> 00:34:30,770
Are you alright?

446
00:34:31,240 --> 00:34:32,240
Okay. We'll take it from here.

447
00:34:35,890 --> 00:34:39,520
Great!

448
00:34:40,410 --> 00:34:41,680
Let it rain!

449
00:34:42,370 --> 00:34:44,600
Good!

450
00:34:47,970 --> 00:34:48,290
Move!

451
00:34:53,490 --> 00:34:56,560
Heaven, please look at Lanyang.

452
00:35:00,640 --> 00:35:01,120
Sir,

453
00:35:01,600 --> 00:35:03,450
if it still doesn't rain in three days,

454
00:35:04,080 --> 00:35:05,290
won't everyone be even more upset?

455
00:35:06,240 --> 00:35:07,680
What if they blame you

456
00:35:08,080 --> 00:35:09,410
and tear down the County Office?

457
00:35:24,660 --> 00:35:29,260
♪I gaze at high peaks
and sails far away♪

458
00:35:29,760 --> 00:35:32,960
♪With the world in my heart,
I leave the shore♪

459
00:35:33,930 --> 00:35:38,960
♪Frost on my shoulders,
joys and sorrows stretch afar♪

460
00:35:39,330 --> 00:35:42,560
♪A thousand miles of lights
keep me company♪

461
00:35:43,900 --> 00:35:48,530
♪By noon, the mist will lift;
rivers will bend♪

462
00:35:48,930 --> 00:35:52,060
♪Today, lean on the rail with me again♪

463
00:35:53,460 --> 00:35:58,640
♪Tread the boundless clouds
and rise with the wind♪

464
00:35:59,070 --> 00:36:01,880
♪March to the gates
with fearless hearts♪

465
00:36:06,020 --> 00:36:11,890
♪Break every gate♪

466
00:36:38,370 --> 00:36:38,770
Sir.

467
00:36:38,930 --> 00:36:39,770
The wind's picking up.

468
00:36:39,970 --> 00:36:40,490
Sir.

469
00:36:40,930 --> 00:36:41,640
The wind's picking up!

470
00:36:49,780 --> 00:36:52,420
(Chengfu Gate)

471
00:36:52,960 --> 00:36:58,020
♪Be the ferry
where you wait for the sun♪

472
00:37:00,120 --> 00:37:05,220
♪Be the blue silk
that catches your tears♪

473
00:37:06,410 --> 00:37:08,370
Heaven, please let it rain!

474
00:37:10,450 --> 00:37:11,640
Please, let it rain!

475
00:37:13,660 --> 00:37:18,420
♪Let's conspire to grow old together♪

476
00:37:19,370 --> 00:37:21,930
Please send us some rain!

477
00:37:21,970 --> 00:37:25,873
♪Let me be a captive beast
bound by the same lock as you♪

478
00:37:27,520 --> 00:37:33,630
♪- Through trails of mud and blood
- Let grief drown in your eyes♪

479
00:37:35,180 --> 00:37:38,393
♪- Soar with the wind;
- Plunge into hellfire as one♪

480
00:37:38,393 --> 00:37:40,000
♪Burning bright as a song♪

481
00:37:40,050 --> 00:37:43,440
♪See how roses and green bamboo enchant♪

482
00:37:44,060 --> 00:37:47,320
♪Be the vow I make with all my heart♪

483
00:37:49,350 --> 00:37:52,720
♪If we say forever,
then forever it shall be♪

484
00:37:53,860 --> 00:37:56,170
♪Not a single hour less♪

485
00:37:56,220 --> 00:38:02,930
♪However deep the snow,
I'll wait if you're there♪

486
00:38:03,780 --> 00:38:07,100
♪We'll be gods above,
or wandering souls♪

487
00:38:07,300 --> 00:38:10,760
♪In heaven or the underworld,
you're all I need♪

488
00:38:10,810 --> 00:38:17,410
♪If we can stay, let's return
to the village of our first meeting♪

489
00:38:18,030 --> 00:38:19,660
♪- May time be free of fear
- Boats rock♪

490
00:38:19,710 --> 00:38:22,450
♪- May time be free of pain
- Lights fade, seasons turn♪

491
00:38:22,500 --> 00:38:24,620
♪You're the only one I need♪

492
00:38:25,280 --> 00:38:32,050
♪Sharp winds or fierce rain,
nothing can break us♪

493
00:38:32,430 --> 00:38:35,550
♪- Be my one and only in this world
- Be my one and only in this life♪

494
00:38:35,960 --> 00:38:37,840
♪My last untouched innocence♪

495
00:38:54,860 --> 00:38:59,690
♪Let me be the fireflies dancing
across your brow♪

496
00:39:02,020 --> 00:39:06,860
♪Let me hold you
whenever the rain falls♪

497
00:39:07,720 --> 00:39:11,641
♪- Together we'll soar to the skies;
- Together we'll turn to ashes♪

498
00:39:11,641 --> 00:39:14,540
♪- Burning bright as a song;
- Two shadows entwined♪

499
00:39:15,720 --> 00:39:17,370
Let the clouds gather.

500
00:39:19,160 --> 00:39:20,810
Let the rain pour.

501
00:39:22,450 --> 00:39:24,010
May the crops flourish.

502
00:39:25,770 --> 00:39:27,680
The rain-praying ceremony is complete.

503
00:39:27,722 --> 00:39:29,640
♪Not a single hour less♪

504
00:39:29,690 --> 00:39:36,400
♪However deep the snow,
I'll wait if you're there♪

505
00:39:37,250 --> 00:39:40,570
♪We'll be gods above,
or wandering souls♪

506
00:39:40,770 --> 00:39:44,230
♪In heaven or the underworld,
you're all I need♪

507
00:39:44,280 --> 00:39:50,880
♪If we're lucky to stay in this world,
let's return to when we first met♪

508
00:39:51,500 --> 00:39:53,130
♪- May time be free of fear
- Boats rock♪

509
00:39:53,180 --> 00:39:55,920
♪- May time be free of pain
- Lights fade, seasons turn♪

510
00:39:55,970 --> 00:39:58,090
♪You're the only one I need♪

511
00:39:58,750 --> 00:40:05,520
♪Sharp winds or fierce rain,
nothing can break us♪

512
00:40:05,900 --> 00:40:09,020
♪- Be my one and only in this world
- Be my one and only in this life♪

513
00:40:09,430 --> 00:40:11,310
♪My last untouched innocence♪

514
00:40:12,920 --> 00:40:16,160
♪If only we could return
to the village where we first met♪

515
00:40:16,360 --> 00:40:19,760
♪Stay by me; help me forget
the frozen dream of last night♪

516
00:40:19,960 --> 00:40:24,790
♪Fireflies glow, flowers kiss our lips;
just us♪

517
00:40:25,140 --> 00:40:27,060
♪Through dawn and dusk♪

518
00:40:27,180 --> 00:40:28,810
♪- May time be free of fear
- Boats rock♪

519
00:40:28,860 --> 00:40:31,600
♪- May time be free of pain
- Lights fade, seasons turn♪

520
00:40:31,650 --> 00:40:33,770
♪You're the only one I need♪

521
00:40:34,430 --> 00:40:41,200
♪By your side, through joy and pain,
is that eternity?♪

522
00:40:41,580 --> 00:40:44,700
♪- Till fireworks flood the town
- Till the lake is still and clear♪

523
00:40:45,110 --> 00:40:46,990
♪The wind blows past us♪

524
00:40:48,960 --> 00:40:52,490
♪- If there's still
- Some warmth left in this world♪

525
00:40:53,820 --> 00:40:56,890
♪You're the only one I need♪

526
00:41:07,450 --> 00:41:07,930
Yan Shang!

527
00:41:09,330 --> 00:41:09,810
Yan Shang.

528
00:41:12,370 --> 00:41:12,930
Yan Shang!

529
00:41:45,320 --> 00:41:49,160
♪- If there's still
- Some warmth left in this world♪

530
00:41:50,460 --> 00:41:52,920
♪You're the only one I need♪

531
00:42:36,720 --> 00:42:38,490
Something this serious happened,
and you didn't tell me.

532
00:42:40,040 --> 00:42:41,080
I ought to slap you.

533
00:42:42,850 --> 00:42:43,640
Wanyao.

534
00:42:49,240 --> 00:42:49,850
Wanyao.

535
00:42:52,640 --> 00:42:53,450
Wanyao.

536
00:42:54,850 --> 00:42:55,850
I'm so cold.

537
00:42:57,970 --> 00:42:58,970
It hurts.

538
00:43:05,490 --> 00:43:06,640
Can I

539
00:43:08,200 --> 00:43:09,450
stop walking now?

540
00:43:10,450 --> 00:43:10,930
Okay.

541
00:43:12,450 --> 00:43:13,010
No more walking.

542
00:43:14,010 --> 00:43:14,600
Your Highness.

543
00:43:16,930 --> 00:43:17,850
Your Highness.

544
00:43:18,890 --> 00:43:19,720
I killed someone.

545
00:43:20,450 --> 00:43:21,330
I can't escape.

546
00:43:27,970 --> 00:43:28,490
Don't be afraid.

547
00:43:29,080 --> 00:43:29,930
I can't escape.

548
00:43:30,770 --> 00:43:31,290
Yan Shang.

549
00:43:33,970 --> 00:43:35,120
You've made it through.

550
00:43:41,490 --> 00:43:42,040
Your Highness.

551
00:44:13,080 --> 00:44:13,770
Wanyao.

552
00:44:14,970 --> 00:44:15,520
Wanyao.

553
00:44:16,720 --> 00:44:17,410
I'm here.

554
00:44:19,600 --> 00:44:20,120
Yan Shang.

555
00:44:22,010 --> 00:44:22,520
Sleep.

556
00:44:34,240 --> 00:44:34,890
Don't go.

557
00:44:37,010 --> 00:44:37,450
Don't go.

558
00:44:59,500 --> 00:45:03,740
(Next Episode Preview)

559
00:45:04,160 --> 00:45:04,850
The truth is...

560
00:45:05,330 --> 00:45:06,200
I'm scared.

561
00:45:06,810 --> 00:45:07,720
Because even in my dreams,

562
00:45:08,290 --> 00:45:10,490
your face is starting to fade.

563
00:45:11,120 --> 00:45:11,680
If

564
00:45:12,160 --> 00:45:13,240
I could see you just once more,

565
00:45:14,010 --> 00:45:15,080
I'd remember it all.

566
00:45:15,970 --> 00:45:17,490
Every detail of your face.

567
00:45:20,961 --> 00:45:24,254
♪Be the ferry
where you wait for the sun♪

568
00:45:26,939 --> 00:45:31,855
♪Be the blue silk
that catches your tears♪

569
00:45:34,049 --> 00:45:39,894
♪Be the sleeve we held,
worn by dust and years♪

570
00:45:40,394 --> 00:45:45,620
♪Let's conspire to grow old together♪

571
00:45:48,389 --> 00:45:53,180
♪Let me be a captive beast
bound by the same lock as you♪

572
00:45:54,016 --> 00:46:00,095
♪- Through trails of mud and blood;
- let grief drown in your eyes♪

573
00:46:01,896 --> 00:46:05,046
♪Soar with the wind;
plunge into hellfire as one♪

574
00:46:05,046 --> 00:46:06,694
♪Burning bright as a song♪

575
00:46:06,746 --> 00:46:10,470
♪See how roses and green bamboo enchant♪

576
00:46:10,848 --> 00:46:15,514
♪Be the vow I make with all my heart♪

577
00:46:16,133 --> 00:46:20,174
♪If we say forever,
then forever it shall be♪

578
00:46:20,665 --> 00:46:22,780
♪Not a single hour less♪

579
00:46:22,820 --> 00:46:29,766
♪However deep the snow,
I'll wait if you're there♪

580
00:46:30,529 --> 00:46:33,982
♪We'll be gods above,
or wandering souls♪

581
00:46:34,162 --> 00:46:37,307
♪In heaven or the underworld,
you're all I need♪

582
00:46:37,746 --> 00:46:44,383
♪If we can stay, let's return
to the village of our first meeting♪

583
00:46:44,780 --> 00:46:46,818
♪- May time be free of fear;
- boats rock♪

584
00:46:46,818 --> 00:46:49,294
♪- May time be free of pain;
- lights fade, seasons turn♪

585
00:46:49,332 --> 00:46:51,801
♪You're the only one I need♪

586
00:46:52,005 --> 00:46:58,892
♪Sharp winds or fierce rain,
nothing can break us♪

587
00:46:59,204 --> 00:47:02,475
♪Be mine in this world;
be mine in this life♪

588
00:47:02,780 --> 00:47:05,953
♪My last untouched innocence♪

589
00:47:06,277 --> 00:47:09,703
♪If only we could return
to the village where we first met♪

590
00:47:09,936 --> 00:47:13,161
♪Stay by me; help me forget
the frozen dream of last night♪

591
00:47:13,492 --> 00:47:20,288
♪Fireflies glow, flowers kiss our lips;
just us, through dawn and dusk♪

592
00:47:20,657 --> 00:47:22,719
♪- May time be free of fear;
- boats rock♪

593
00:47:22,720 --> 00:47:25,223
♪- May time be free of pain;
- lights fade, seasons turn♪

594
00:47:25,270 --> 00:47:27,608
♪You're the only one I need♪

595
00:47:27,839 --> 00:47:34,674
♪By your side, through joy and pain,
is that eternity?♪

596
00:47:35,023 --> 00:47:36,641
♪Till fireworks flood the town♪

597
00:47:36,771 --> 00:47:38,567
♪Till the lake is still and clear♪

598
00:47:38,924 --> 00:47:41,941
♪You're the only one I need♪

599
00:47:41,981 --> 00:47:43,308
(No animals were harmed
or mistreated in production.)

